<!--
    The ONLY user-facing strings that live in Android resources. Everything else is in
    app/src/main/java/com/volume_plus_plus/app/i18n/Strings.kt — see docs/TRANSLATING.md.

    These are different because *Android* renders them, not us: the launcher draws app_name, the
    accessibility-service label and description are shown by system Settings, and qs_tile_label names
    the tile in the Quick Settings picker — all read straight out of our APK. There is no way to hand
    the OS an in-app override, so they are translated the platform's way — values-es/, values-pt/,
    values-fr/ — and follow the *device* language rather than the app's language setting.

    qs_tile_label is the only one we get a second bite at: once the tile has been placed,
    VolumePanelTileService renames it from Strings.kt, so a tile already on screen does follow the
    app's language. The picker entry can't.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">Volume++</string>
    <string name="volume_key_service_label">Volume++ overlay</string>
    <string name="volume_key_service_description">Lets Volume++ show its own volume panel with per-app sliders when you press the volume keys, replacing the system panel.</string>
    <string name="qs_tile_label">Volume Panel</string>
</resources>
